    "rule": "Split the word into two to four UniDic noun, na-adjective, prefix, or suffix rows by spelling and kana form, keeping the splits with the fewest parts; combine the parts by UniDic's accent combination types, moving a downstep off a special mora within a part. The splits with the fewest parts that give a value must all agree; a split that gives no value is left out. Ship the value only in a shipped group. Where the rule gives none, a two-part kanji compound whose second part is C2 keeps that rule's downstep, on the second part's first mora.",
